  aa.sv  § pkgTypespecInstanceIsTop (ParamEmit drainDefParamTs, beside the
        existing topPkgView arm).  A MODULE parameter typed by a PACKAGE ENUM
        typedef (`parameter prim_pkg::impl_e Impl = prim_pkg::ImplGeneric;`)
        binds the ELABORATED (uhdmtopPackages) typespec object, not the
        def-listing one — exactly the rule makeTypespec already applies to
        every real SIGNAL use (TypeEmit's pkgTopTypedefTs preference at ~346);
        parameters were the outlier.  THE OBJECTS ARE TEXT-IDENTICAL IN A DUMP:
        they differ only in which package copy their vpiInstance names, and
        instance::Compare reads VpiTop, so the head reads "r=1 failLhs=package
        {top=1} failRhs=package {top=0}" with NOTHING visible in a diff.  The
        pointer-identity probe (r10earl4t) is how it was seen at all.  14
        Earlgrey heads on prim_pkg (which holds NOTHING but `typedef enum
        integer {ImplGeneric, ImplXilinx} impl_e`) + 3 on prim_cipher_pkg.

  aa.sv  § pkgEnumParamDefRhs (ParamEmit ~11887, beside modPkgRefIntTsRhs9).
        The SAME parameter's DEF-view param_assign Rhs constant carries (a) the
        enum member's OWN constType — golden reads ct 7 / INT:0 / "0" where we
        minted ct 9, because ExprEmit's qualified-enum fold (~3556) maps every
        `INT:` enum value to vpiUIntConst — and (b) a ref_typespec at the SCOPE
        PREFIX (`work@am`, not `work@am.Impl`) bound to the enum typespec.  The
        ELAB view was already right: it takes § enumConstOvEnc, which is
        topView-only.  13 heads (prim_ram_1p, prim_ram_2p, prim_rom,
        prim_clock_gating, prim_clock_mux2, prim_flash, prim_pad_wrapper,
        padctrl — every `PRIM_DEFAULT_IMPL` module).  The free-standing fold is
        NOT touched: golden keeps ct 9 for the same shape inside a cont-assign
        operation (alert_handler_ping_timer:140).

  bb.sv/ee.sv  § genRefModuleImplicitPort (ModuleEmit ~22122, the SYNTAX-driven
        gen-block instantiation loop).  The `.name` SHORTHAND (`.clk_i,` — no
        parentheses, no actual; LRM 23.3.2.3) is a REAL connection: golden
        lists it as a NAMED port with no high_conn at the connection's own
        span.  We dropped it together with the `.douta ()` EMPTY form, which is
        the anonymous one.  Every Earlgrey gen-scope child read "golden
        ports=N, ours=N-2" and the two missing rows were always `.clk_i` /
        `.rst_ni` — ref_module::Compare reports that as "r=1 failLhs=the
        ref_module itself" (the vector-size arm).  14 heads (tlul_socket_1n
        gen_dfifo/fifo_d 7, prim_diff_decode gen_async/i_sync_p 5, gpio
        gen_filter/filter, nmi_gen gen_esc_sev).  ee.sv is BYTE-IDENTICAL.

  ff.sv  § genRefModuleWildcardConn (same loop).  A `.*` connection is ONE
        NAMELESS port whose High_conn is a constant carrying VpiValue
        "STRING:.*" / VpiDecompile ".*" and NO size and NO constType, spanning
        the connection node (Surelog CompileHelper:2946).  The AST
        instantiation path already built it (findWildcardConn / wcS9); this
        syntax path skipped every non-NamedPortConnection, so a gen-scope child
        instantiated with a bare `.*` came out with an EMPTY port vector.
        13 heads — again every `PRIM_DEFAULT_IMPL` module, whose implementation
        child is always `prim_generic_x u_impl_generic (.*);` inside `if (1)
        begin : gen_generic` or an `Impl == ImplXilinx` if/else pair.

  gg.sv/hh.sv  § impCopyBasedDecKeep (ParamEmit ~11525: `topView` ->
        `topView && !defViewOrig9` on the DEC-based re-render).  "The DEF view
        keeps DEC" means the PHYSICAL def view.  § modDefImportShape
        force-flips topView for a module DEF-view MATERIALIZED IMPORT copy and
        the flip leaked into this rule, so ibex_alu — a module WITH a parameter
        port list, hence flipped — listed ibex_pkg's `parameter logic [1:0]
        CSR_MISA_MXL = 2'd1` as INT `1` in its AllModules entry, while
        ibex_compressed_decoder (no port list, no flip) was already right.
        Four-base x four-view matrix (hh.sv, one package read by a
        port-list child and a port-list-less one):
            base     pkg DEF   pkg TOP   mod DEF   ELAB INSTANCE
            2'd1     DEC       DEC       DEC       INT 1        <- respells
            4'o7     OCT       OCT       OCT       UINT 7       <- respells
            4'h2     HEX       HEX       HEX       HEX 4'h2
            4'b1010  BIN       BIN       BIN       BIN 4'b1010
        i.e. DEC->INT and OCT->UINT happen in the ELABORATED INSTANCE ONLY.
        12 heads (ibex_alu, ibex_controller, ibex_core, ibex_cs_registers,
        ibex_decoder, ibex_ex_block, ibex_id_stage, ibex_if_stage,
        ibex_multdiv_fast, ibex_pmp, ibex_wb_stage, ...).  NOTE the OCT row is
        a residue, not a law we implemented — see (5) below.

