LANDED — PASS 5 (r10earl5; every law gated at goldens 23/23 + u2r testflags
0 change + Surelog both-modes 0 change INCLUDING the dump column — three full
gate rounds).  Earlgrey_0_1 stays CMP_NOTEQUAL (groundwork), census below.

  THE PWRMGR/RSTMGR/ALERT/FLASH PACKAGE FAMILY — pass 4's ranked residue (2),
  6 AllPackages + 5 TopPackages heads and 7 parentless ref_typespec module
  heads — IS ONE ROW.  The chain, decoded with r10earl5ts + r10earl5op:
  typespec::Compare recurses Instance(), so comparing ANY of pwrmgr_pkg's 16
  typespecs re-compares the whole package; every one of them, and every
  pattern row 5..12, reported the SAME head; and the head "failLhs
  ref_typespec 0:0 / failRhs <null>" is the pattern operation's own Typespec
  ref on ROW 12 ALONE (PWR_PERI_DEFAULT, pwrmgr_pkg.sv:155).  The other rows
  were already equal and were only echoing it.  Two laws close it:

  jj.sv  § symDimScopedRefFlat (ParamEmit ~8695, the SYMBOLIC-DIM rule).  That
        rule ("a struct whose member carries a parameter-dependent packed
        dimension never flattens in either home-package view") is real but
        does NOT outrank the SCOPED-REFERENCE rule beside it.  `pkg::NAME`
        written anywhere outside a parameter declaration is the trigger
        Surelog's substituteAssignedValue runs off, and it TYPES the pattern op
        — the flatten's precondition — whatever the member dims look like.
        pwrmgr_pkg pins both halves in one file: of its eight struct-pattern
        parameters, FIVE are read as `pwrmgr_pkg::X` from top_earlgrey.sv's
        port connections (rows 5/8/9/10/12) and golden flattens exactly those
        five; the three read only unqualified or not at all (rows 6/7/11) keep
        the tagged tree.  Row 12 is `pwr_peri_t`, whose members are
        `logic [WakeUpPeris-1:0]` / `logic [HwRstReqs-1:0]` — symbolic — and
        golden flattens it anyway.  The symbolic-dim witnesses
        (MultiConcatValueSize & family, pinmux_pkg::DefaultTargetCfg) read
        their parameter UNQUALIFIED after a wildcard import, so they never had
        a scoped ref to be exempted by — checked before the change, 0 movers
        after it.

  jj.sv  § patMemberCastNoDecomp (ParamEmit ~9470, the flat-walk member fold)
        + § patMemberSizeCastDef (ExprEmit ~10766, the DEF-view tagged member).
        A member value written as a CAST folds with NO VpiDecompile at all —
        Surelog answers a cast out of ExprEval (value + width) and never
        re-renders source text for it.  The two views disagree about the WIDTH
        and that is the whole subtlety; jj.sv is one row per spelling, read
        side by side (member `logic [15:0]`):
            source                   DEF listing        TOP (flattened)
            WakeUpPeris'(1'b1)     UINT:1 sz16 dec ''  UINT:1 sz16 dec ''
            16'(1'b1)              UINT:1 sz16 dec ''  UINT:1 sz16 dec ''
            8'(1'b1)               UINT:1 sz 8 dec ''  UINT:1 sz16 dec ''
            WakeUpPeris'(HwRstReqs) UINT:2 sz16 dec '' UINT:2 sz16 dec ''
            16'(16'h1)             UINT:1 sz16 dec ''  UINT:1 sz16 dec ''
        i.e. the DEF view keeps the CAST's own width, the elaborated view
        re-sizes to the MEMBER's.  CONTROLS in the same package, all matching
        already and all keeping their digits: `'1` -> "65535", `'0` -> "0",
        `16'h1` and `2'b10` keep their source form.
        THE <=64 CEILING IS REGRESSION-DERIVED, not a guess: the first cut
        moved u2r ImportedDoubleCastedParameter (`Prefix:
        96'(96'h 4c52_5443_5f4d_4f52_4001_0001)`) from CMP_EQUAL to
        CMP_NOTEQUAL — golden keeps that whole vpiCastOp tree.  jj.sv's
        `16'(16'h1)` row folds, so a BASED-LITERAL operand is NOT the blocker;
        the width is (Surelog's ExprEval answers in 64 bits).

  ll.sv  § impArithFoldSigned (ParamEmit ~10510, `intForm7`) + the new
        file-scope srlgArithFoldSigned beside containsPatternOrConcat.  A
        DEF-view MATERIALIZED IMPORT copy of a package localparam with an
        ARITHMETIC init was unconditionally INT.  It is reduced by the SAME
        ExprEval the elaborated listings use, so it obeys the per-OPERATOR
        signedness rule already decoded at § foldSigned9: `+` and `<<` come
        back UINT, `-` `*` `/` and unary minus INT, and a signed operand
        propagates up through `+`.  ll.sv is one package, one importing module
        (`module m import lp::*;`, the pwrmgr_wake_info shape), one localparam
        per operator, read across ALL FOUR listings:
            WakeUpPeris + 2   ALLPKG op / TOPPKG UINT / ALLMOD UINT / TOPMOD UINT
            WakeUpPeris - 4   ALLPKG op / TOPPKG INT  / ALLMOD INT  / TOPMOD INT
            WakeUpPeris * 2   ALLPKG op / TOPPKG INT  / ALLMOD INT  / TOPMOD INT
            12 (no fold)      UINT everywhere
            int W = X + 1     TOPPKG UINT / ALLMOD UINT / TOPMOD UINT
        Only ALLMOD was wrong, and only on the two `+` rows.  5 Earlgrey heads,
        all ONE object: pwrmgr_pkg.sv:19 `localparam TotalWakeWidth =
        WakeUpPeris + 2` in pwrmgr / pwrmgr_cdc / pwrmgr_fsm / pwrmgr_slow_fsm
        / pwrmgr_wake_info.  srlgArithFoldSigned adds `/` (which § foldSigned9's
        switch omits despite its own matrix recording `100/5 -> INT`) because
        HierPathStructTypespec's `(Sha3Latency + RegLatency - 1)/RegLatency`
        has `/` at the top and must stay INT; § foldSigned9 itself is left
        alone.

  mm.sv  § unpackedElemVecTypedef (ParamEmit makeUnpackedArrayParamTs ~12810).
        An UNPACKED-ARRAY parameter whose ELEMENT type is spelled as a VECTOR
        TYPEDEF binds that typedef's typespec, not a fresh anonymous one.  The
        arm above it already did this for struct / union / enum typedefs;
        `typedef logic [31:0] sha_word_t;` + `localparam sha_word_t InitHash
        [8]` fell through to the mint-fresh path, so golden's Elem_typespec
        pointed at `logic_typespec 'sha_word_t' hmac_pkg.sv:17:11` and ours at
        an anonymous one born at the declaration (:26:14).
        TWO distinguishers, both measured on mm.sv:
        (a) the rule keys on the DECLARED TYPE SYNTAX, not the resolved type —
            row B writes the identical shape longhand (`localparam logic [31:0]
            RawHash [4]`) and golden gives THAT one an anonymous element
            typespec, so only a TypeAlias element takes the bind;
        (b) the object bound is § LAW S's BARE copy (`sha_word_t` + a
            Typedef_alias ref to `mp::sha_word_t`), not the qualified package
            table entry — the first cut bound the table entry and the head
            moved from "anonymous vs named" to "'sha_word_t' vs
            'mp::sha_word_t'".  bareScalarTdCopyOf(ts, true) is that copy; the
            design-final rebind that implements LAW S does not reach an
            array_typespec's Elem_typespec.
        4 of the 6 Earlgrey sha_word_t heads (all the AllModules ones) plus
        mm.sv's TopPackages head.  PARTIAL, deliberately: the package's own DEF
        listing (AllPackages) still mints the anonymous element — that view
        emits its parameters BEFORE its typedefs, so typedefTs has no entry to
        find yet.  Ranked as residue (1) below with the witness in hand.

