        hmac_pkg's last sha_word_t head; mm.sv is now cmp-EQUAL.

  nn.sv  § deferredPortUnpackedArrayTs (ModuleEmit materializeDefNetTs).  The
        DEFERRED half of "EVERY DEF-view UNPACKED-array port wraps its element
        ts in an array_typespec" (emitPorts, r10c5).  A port whose PACKED range
        names an OVERRIDABLE parameter — `input [DW-1:0] data_i [N]` — does not
        build its def typespec inline: rangeRefsOverriddenParam parks a bare
        ref_typespec and materializeDefNetTs unfolds it in the write phase, and
        THAT path never wrapped.  The port came out carrying the ELEMENT
        logic_typespec alone, stretched over the whole declaration (unpacked
        dim included) instead of an array_typespec over the element.  The gate
        is the whole story: the same declaration WITHOUT a parameter in its
        packed range (`input sel_i [N]`, nn.sv row C) took the inline arm and
        was already right.  NETS are not wrapped in either path (golden gives
        the def-view net of `logic [5:0] p [32]` a plain logic_typespec), so
        the new arm keys on the parked ref_typespec's parent being the PORT.
        9 Earlgrey heads read "array_typespec vs logic_typespec" at exactly
        this shape.

  oo.sv  § unknownModuleRefPorts (ModuleEmit, the def-view ref_module loop's
        UninstantiatedDef arm).  Pass 5 ranked this "DECODED, ready to
        implement" and it was half-true: we DO emit the stub (name, `work@<T>`
        defname, null Actual) but with an EMPTY port vector, and
        ref_module::Compare reports that as the ref_module itself.  Golden
        carries the WRITTEN connection list — one port per connection, named
        after the FORMAL, spanning the whole `.F (actual)` node, the actual as
        High_conn under the scope <prefix>.<inst>.<formal>; a literal actual
        stays UNPARENTED.  slang has no port list to walk (there is no
        definition), so the connections come off the instantiation SYNTAX and
        each actual is bound in the INSTANTIATING scope.
        WITNESS SHAPE MATTERS: slang REJECTS `BUFGCE u_bufgce(...)` outright
        wherever it elaborates the instantiation, and leaving the enclosing
        module uninstantiated does not help — slang then promotes it to a TOP
        and the error comes back.  The Earlgrey trio survive only because
        prim_xilinx_* are instantiated ONLY in an untaken `Impl == ImplXilinx`
        arm, so oo.sv has to do the same.  3 heads (BUFGCE / BUFGMUX / IOBUF);
        oo.sv is cmp-EQUAL, 5 dump lines left (parenting only).

  hh.sv  § sizedOctElabRespell (ParamEmit ~11525, beside pass 4's
        § impCopyBasedDecKeep).  Pass 4 measured the four-base x four-view
        matrix and implemented only its DEC half.  OCTAL JOINS DECIMAL in the
        ELABORATED INSTANCE exactly as § unsizedBasedTypedParamElab already
        records for the UNSIZED spelling (`'o10` -> UINT 8): `4'o7` reads OCT
        in the package DEF, the package TOP and BOTH module DEF listings and
        `7 / UINT:7 / size 4` in the elab instance, while `4'h2` and `4'b1010`
        never respell in any view.  x/z digits keep their octal form (no
        decimal spelling), the same carve-out the unsized arm makes.

  pp.sv  § liveCallEntryIsContAssignRhs (ExprEmit ~7062 + ModuleEmit ~16252)
        and § pkgBodyArgTsCalledAsCaRhs (ExprEmit argCtxOk) + the new
        § pkgSubEvaluatedFromParamInit9 (TaskFuncEmit).  THE BIGGEST REMAINING
        CLASS — 11 AllModules heads + 2 TopPackages, all reading
        "failLhs <null> / failRhs ref_typespec '' 0:0" under
        `operation -> func_call aes_mul_gf2p2 -> assignment -> function
        aes_mul_gf2p4 -> package aes_sbox_canright_pkg`, i.e. WE stamp a
        formal-typespec ref on a func-call argument that golden leaves bare.
        The rule is not about the argument at all: a function BODY carries its
        formal-ts stamps only when Surelog's evaluator actually RAN it, and the
        shapes that run it are the ones § subCalledAsContAssignRhs already
        names — a call that IS the whole rhs of a continuous assignment — plus
        a call in a PARAMETER INITIALISER.  pp.sv reads both halves in one
        file: golden stamps every operation actual inside FuncArgs' `pow_a`
        (`assign out1 = pow_a(inp, 3);`) and NOT ONE anywhere in pp.sv, where
        the identical package function, the identical module-local function
        and a byte-for-byte copy of pow_a itself are all called as operands of
        a `^`.  Two sites had to move: the liveCalledSubs ENTRY POINT (which
        counted any call outside a body) and the pkgTopEmit arm of argCtxOk
        (which stamped every elaborated package body unconditionally).
        THE REGRESSION IS THE DISTINGUISHER: the first cut was cont-assign-only
        and moved EvalFunc from CMP_EQUAL to CMP_NOTEQUAL — its
        `localparam log2RATIO4 = prim_util_pkg::vbits(RATIO);` is a package
        function evaluated from a PARAMETER INIT.  § subEvaluatedFromParamInit
        models that already but keys on the subroutine's own InstanceBody,
        which a package function does not have, so
        § pkgSubEvaluatedFromParamInit9 is its design-wide sibling.

  qq.sv  § genConnOperatorActual (ModuleEmit, the def-view gen-block
        instantiation loop + two syntax-keyed op maps in EmitHelpers.h).  That
        loop TEXT-PARSES its port actuals and had arms for selects, ranges,
        calls, literals and concats; every other shape fell into the final else
        and became ONE ref_obj NAMED with the raw source text — `~clk_i` came
        out as a ref_obj literally called "~clk_i", with that string in its
        fullname.  Golden builds an operation whose operands are formal-scoped
        refs, exactly like the concat arm beside it.  Measured on qq.sv, three
        rows in one gen block: `~clk_i` -> vpiBitNegOp with operand ref_obj
        `clk_i` scoped <branch>.<inst>.<formal>.clk_i; `clk_i & b_i` ->
        vpiBitAndOp, both operands scoped the same way; `!b_i` -> vpiNotOp.
        3 heads (prim_clock_inverter:18 and the dmi_jtag / dmi_jtag_tap that
        instantiate it).

  ss.sv  § modParamCastBindScope (ParamEmit ~3288).  A size cast written in a
        MODULE parameter DEFAULT could not reach the decoded parameter-width
        cast model at all: that whole region sits behind
        `else if (currentScope || castBindScope)` and NEITHER is set while a
        module's parameter port list is emitted — castBindScope was published
        for `inPackage` only.  So `parameter logic [SDw-1:0] Seed = SDw'(1)`
        fell to the catch-all logic_typespec at the cast tokens where golden
        has the named int_typespec at the WIDTH PARAMETER's own name token
        (a zero-width span) carrying its folded value.  ss.sv is the matrix:
        `int unsigned SDw = 32` -> int_typespec 'SDw' 13:29..13:29 UINT:32; an
        UNTYPED `SN = 4` and a signed `int SI = 6` the same; the literal-sized
        control `8'(1)` keeps the integer_typespec arm.  2 heads (prim_lfsr:39
        DefaultSeed, ibex_dummy_instr).

  rr.sv  NEGATIVE WITNESS, kept deliberately — it does NOT reproduce.  The 4
        remaining AllPackages heads are all one written shape (a package
        localparam whose initialiser reads ANOTHER package, or its own earlier
        $clog2 localparams: rstmgr_pkg:8 `pwrmgr_pkg::HwRstReqs`,
