THE PASS-8 RANKED-(1) LEAD WAS RIGHT AND IT WAS TWO WRITERS, NOT ONE.  The four
"ref_obj NAMED WITH ITS OWN SOURCE TEXT" singletons split into a SYS-CALL
ARGUMENT emitter (dm_sba, prim_packer, hmac, pinmux — all `$clog2(<expr>)`) and
the DEF-VIEW GEN-BLOCK PORT-ACTUAL dispatcher (ibex_icache, and pinmux's second
head).  Both are the same BUG SHAPE — a text-driven emitter whose final else
names a ref_obj with the raw text — and both are fixed by routing the shape to
the SYNTAX emitter that already builds it.

  ua.sv/ub.sv  § sysCallArgOperatorTree (TypeEmit emitSyntaxExpr, the sys-call
        argument loop).  An OPERATOR- or LITERAL-shaped argument is a real
        expression tree; only a NAME-shaped one is a ref_obj.  Until now
        everything that was not a concatenation, a dotted path or an elab
        splice fell to the raw-text fallback, so `$clog2(N+1)` came out as ONE
        ref_obj literally NAMED "N+1".  Matrix (ub.sv, one
        `logic [$clog2(<arg>)-1:0]` per row, golden left):
            W               ref_obj(W)          (already right)
            64              constant 64/64/ct9  <- was ref_obj("64")
            N+1             operation op24
            (N+1)           operation op24 AT THE INNER SPAN (paren discarded)
            -N              operation op1
            N > 4 ? N : 4   operation op32
            ubp::PW+1       operation op24
            2**N            operation op43
            {4'd3, 4'd2}    operation op33      (already right)
            $bits(my_t) / $bits(ubp::st_t)      ref_obj (type names: right)
        Routed on the UNWRAPPED node, so a parenthesised argument gets the
        inner span golden uses.  ua.sv is BYTE-IDENTICAL.  Corpus: dm_sba.sv:63
        `$clog2(BusWidth/8)`, prim_packer.sv:42 `$clog2(InW+1)`, hmac.sv:309
        `$clog2(32+1)`, pinmux.sv:157 `2**$clog2(NMioPads+2)` — dm_sba and
        prim_packer CLOSED, hmac and pinmux ADVANCED to the bound-fold family.

  ue.sv  § sysCallArgPkgParamSubst (same loop).  A query-call argument that
        NAMES A PACKAGE PARAMETER is SUBSTITUTED by that parameter's own value
        constant — the MODULE-listing half of the package/own split the loop
        already had for package listings.  DISTINGUISHERS, all measured:
          * `$clog2(LP)` with LP a MODULE-LOCAL localparam stays a ref_obj
            (ud.sv proves a module-local bound is NOT folded in ANY position,
            so "localparam" is not the trigger — the HOME PACKAGE is);
          * the substituted object is the package parameter's own constant
            COPIED VERBATIM and re-sized to its declared width, NOT a decimal
            re-render: `parameter logic [2:0] PV = 3'h1` substitutes as
            `3'h1`/HEX:1/ct5/size 3.  Writing UINT:1/"1" instead DEMOTED u2r
            DivisionOfSize (`$bits(PartInvDefault)/1-1`) — measured as a
            regression and then fixed by reusing crossPkgBoundFoldConst9;
          * the TS REF splits on the WRITTEN SPELLING: an UNQUALIFIED
            (wildcard-imported) read carries one, a QUALIFIED `pkg::NAME` read
            carries NONE (ue.sv rows K/N and L/M, all four views).
        Corpus: sha2.sv:36 `logic [$clog2(NumRound)-1:0]` (hmac_pkg::NumRound,
        wildcard-imported).  ue.sv is cmp-EQUAL.

  uc.sv  § modStructMemberPkgFold, QUALIFIED spelling (TypeEmit emitSyntaxExpr
        ScopedName arm).  A struct typedef declared INSIDE a module substitutes
        an imported package parameter in a member's range bound; the BARE
        spelling already did, `pkg::NAME` fell to the ref_obj.  The substituted
        constant is identical (ts ref named after the MEMBER).  The NEGATIVE
        control immediately above it — a `[pkg::WIDTH-1:0]` OUTPUT PORT bound,
        which Surelog leaves unfolded (fail_detect_width) — is untouched: it
        carries no structMemberTsCtx.  Corpus: tlul_adapter_sram.sv:56 `logic
        [top_pkg::TL_SZW-1:0] size ;`.  The constant builder is now the shared
        helper modStructMemberPkgSubst9.

  uc.sv  § pkgBoundFoldBareImport (crossPkgFoldBoundLeaves9 gains a
        `bareScope`).  § crossPkgRangeBoundFold's "the distinguisher is the
        WRITTEN qualification" was too narrow: getValue keys on the NAME, so a
        module that WILDCARD-IMPORTS the package and writes the bare name gets
        the identical fold.  Rows A (a parameter PORT's declared type) and G (a
        localparam's) of uc.sv, both `constant 3/32/UINT ct9` in golden with
        the ts ref named after the parameter being declared; the BARE read
        keeps the identifier's own span where the qualified one truncates to
        the `pkg::` qualifier.  ud.sv is the negative control.  Corpus:
        padring.sv:15 `module padring import padctrl_reg_pkg::*; #(parameter
        logic [NMioPads-1:0] ConnectMioIn = '1, ...)` — 2 heads (AllModules and
        TopModules are the same object).

  uf.sv  § shadowedImportBoundFold (new helper wildcardPkgParamNamed9, used by
        the defNetTsScope bound arm and by the gen_for loop-bound fold).  A
        MODULE-LOCAL declaration of the same name does NOT hide the imported
        package member from Surelog's name-keyed getValue the way it does for
        slang's Lookup.  rv_timer declares `localparam int N_HARTS = 1;` next
        to `import rv_timer_reg_pkg::*;`, which declares `parameter int
        N_HARTS = 1;`, and golden folds every bound that reads it; usbdev is
        the same shape (`localparam int NEndpoints =
        usbdev_reg_pkg::NEndpoints;`).  ud.sv (no same-named import) stays
        symbolic and is the control.

  uf.sv  § genForInitPkgParamFold (ModuleEmit, the def-view gen_for).  The loop
        INIT takes the identical package-parameter fold that until now only the
        CONDITION got; the folder is factored into foldPkgLoopRef1 so a
        TOP-LEVEL ref (not just an operand) folds too.  Corpus: pinmux.sv:222
        `for (genvar k = NDioPads; k < AlignedMuxSize; k++)`.

  ug.sv  § genConnReplCastActual (ModuleEmit, the def-view gen-block
        instantiation's port-actual dispatcher).  Two shapes had no arm and
        fell to the final else, coming out as ONE ref_obj named with the
        actual's source text; both are already built correctly by the SYNTAX
        emitter and only needed the formal-doubled ref scope this loop uses
        everywhere else.  Golden's shapes, read off ug.sv:
            .wmask_i ({TAG_W{1'b1}})       -> operation 34 over
                [count ref @18..23, inner concat op 33 @23..29], outer span
                17..30; the inner constant is 1'b1/BIN/size 1/ct 3
            .mode_i (mode_e'(mode_raw_i))  -> operation 67 with a ref_typespec
                named <branch>.<inst>.<formal> onto an UNSUPPORTED_TYPESPEC
                `mode_e` (the def view resolves no type), operand the operand
                ref scoped through the formal
        Corpus: ibex_icache.sv:311 `.wmask_i ({TAG_SIZE_ECC{1'b1}})` and
        pinmux.sv:240 `.wkup_mode_i ( wkup_mode_e'(...) )` — BOTH CLOSED, and
        ug.sv's AllModules section is 0 heads.

  uf.sv  § defDimPkgParamFold (TypeEmit buildUnpackedRanges).  "A MODULE dim
        ref stays unbound" is right only while the sizing parameter is a MODULE
        one: a PACKAGE parameter has a value at definition-compile time and
        golden substitutes it here as in every packed bound (UINT constant at
        the parameter's own width, ts ref named <defDimRefPrefix>).
        DISTINGUISHER, measured as a REGRESSION and then gated: applying it in
        a PACKAGE listing too (defDimRefPrefix ending in `::`) demoted
        DefaultPatternInt (`pack::V::CNT`) in BOTH modes — that listing keeps
        its ref BOUND to the sized parameter's own Rhs constant.  Corpus:
        rv_plic.sv:41 `output [SRCW-1:0] irq_id_o [NumTarget]`.

