  * ff.sv — a `.*`-derived ref_obj's END COLUMN: golden stops one character
    short of ours (28:7..28:8 for `.*` where we write 28:7..28:9), while the
    anonymous port and its STRING constant use the full 7..9 span on both
    sides.  Span-only, cmp-irrelevant.
  * aa.sv — golden puts the enum parameter's own resolved VALUE (`INT:0`) on
    the `parameter` object in BOTH module views; we leave it unset.
    cmp-irrelevant (parameter::Compare does not read it), byte-identity only.

RANKED RESIDUE (measured after pass 3; SUPERSEDED by the list above — kept for
the distinguishers it records).  Head counts are
AllModules unless stated; most classes are ONE shared object reached from many
entries, so tests-per-fix is the head count.

  (1) 16 ref_typespec — failLhs <null> vs failRhs ref_typespec, chain
      `operation 61:32 -> func_call aes_mul_gf2p2 -> assignment -> function
      aes_mul_gf2p4` (aes_sbox_canright*).  WE EMIT A ts REF WHERE GOLDEN HAS
      NONE, on a func-call argument operation — the v.sv/w.sv residue above is
      the ready witness.
  (2) 14 `package prim_pkg` (prim_pkg.sv:9:1) — a design-shared package head
      masking behind Instance() recursion.  prim_pkg contains NOTHING but
      `typedef enum integer {ImplGeneric, ImplXilinx} impl_e`, so the difference
      is in that enum.  +3 for prim_cipher_pkg.
  (3) 12 constant ibex_pkg.sv:476:38 — the BASED-DECIMAL FOLD DIRECTION carried
      over from pass 2: `parameter logic [1:0] CSR_MISA_MXL = 2'd1;` keeps
      `2'd1` DEC/ct1/sz2 in golden's module-def param_assign; we rewrite to INT
      `1` ct7.  q.sv row 3 is the OPPOSITE case (golden folds, we keep), so the
      two sites must be decoded together.
  (4) 7 ref_module 'fifo_d' tlul_socket_1n.sv:188:7 under `named_begin
      gen_dfifo / gen_for`, + 5 ref_module 'i_sync_p' prim_diff_decode.sv:57:7 —
      def-view gen-scope child stubs.
  (5) 6 logic_typespec 'sha_word_t' hmac_pkg.sv:17:11 vs an ANONYMOUS
      logic_typespec at 26:14 on our side — a package typedef listing pointer.
  (6) singletons: 3 operation prim_clock_inverter.sv:18:16, 3 ref_obj PTRV_W,
      2 int_typespec LfsrDw, and 2+2+2+2 constants (dm_pkg 29:43, padring
      15:20, flash_phy_pkg 43:53, flash_ctrl_pkg 18:36 — the
      crossPkgRangeBoundFold family's remainder), 1 struct_typespec
      tlul_pkg::tl_h2d_t; plus the unchanged TopModules 8 (sram2tlul,
