RANKED RESIDUE AFTER PASS 2 (SUPERSEDED by the list above — kept for the
distinguishers it records).  Head counts are AllModules
unless stated; most classes are ONE shared object reached from many entries, so
tests-per-fix is the head count.

  (1) ALLMODULES POPULATION — 13 MISSING-RHS entries, SIZE 190 vs 177.
      TRIAGED THIS PASS and it is NOT a dropped construct: `SLANG_UHDM_UNSUP_LOC=1`
      on the whole design reports exactly one kind ("expression kind: Invalid")
      and no module.  The 13 are
        aes_sbox_canright, aes_sbox_canright_masked,
        aes_sbox_canright_masked_noreuse,        (SBoxImpl generate arm)
        ibex_dummy_instr, ibex_icache, ibex_multdiv_slow,   (ibex config params)
        prim_secded_28_22_dec/enc, prim_secded_72_64_dec/enc,  (ECC params)
        prim_xilinx_clock_gating, prim_xilinx_clock_mux2,
        prim_xilinx_pad_wrapper                   (Impl == ImplXilinx arm)
      — every one is IN the .scr file list and is instantiated only inside a
      generate branch that is not taken.  THE LAW: Surelog's uhdmallModules is
      a listing of every module DEFINITION in the compilation, instantiated or
      not; we list only what slang elaborates.  Fix direction: walk
      comp.getDefinitions() (or the syntax trees' ModuleDeclarations) and emit
      a DEF-view entry for the unreferenced ones too.  Biggest single chunk and
      it is a population fix, not a per-object one.

  (2) `'0` NOT EXPANDED IN A PACKAGE — 12 heads (+1 TopPackages).
      aes_pkg.sv:152:15.  golden: ct=3 size=128, decompile = 128 literal '0'
      characters (the fill EXPANDED to the context width); ours: `'0` at size
      -1.  One package object reached from 12 module def entries.

  (3) BASED-DECIMAL FOLD DIRECTION — 12 heads.
      golden keeps `2'd1` (DEC, ct 1); we rewrite to INT `1` (ct 7), in a
      module-def param_assign.  NOTE the opposite is ALSO true elsewhere: q.sv
      row 3 (`hitd = (a[3:0] == rp::DEC3)` reading `parameter logic [3:0] DEC3
      = 4'd 3`) has golden folding to INT `3` where we keep `4'd3`.  So the
      DEC-based rewrite is CONTEXT-dependent and the two sites (ParamEmit's
      elab param rewrite and ExprEmit's ~3251 pkg-param body fold) currently
      disagree with golden in OPPOSITE directions — decode them together.

  (4) 15 `package vs package` heads with the chain `<design>` — a design-shared
      package head masking behind Instance() recursion; one of them is the
      k.sv law:  A PACKAGE PARAMETER READ FROM ANOTHER PACKAGE has its own
      DEF-view value constant RE-SIZED to its declared width (top_pkg's
      `localparam int TL_AW=32` reads back at 32, not 64, once tlul_pkg's
      `logic [top_pkg::TL_AW-1:0]` struct member reads it; a MODULE read does
      not do this — i.sv).  Surelog's getValue returns the package's own
      object (not a clone) for that path and adjustSize mutates it in place.
      k.sv is the ready repro (its ONLY head).

  (5) 13 `operation vs operation` and 6 `constant vs ref_obj <operation/range>`
      — more range-bound folding, now inside net/var and port dims.

  (6) 8 + 3 `ref_typespec vs <null>` (we emit nothing where golden has a ts
      ref), 5 `array_typespec vs logic_typespec <port/module_inst>`,
      5 `ref_module vs ref_module <named_begin/gen_if_else>`,
      4 `ref_obj vs <null> <int_typespec/parameter>`.

  (7) TopModules singletons: prim_keccak operation, prim_present /
      prim_prince `logic_var vs <null>` in a gen_scope_array, jtag_mux,
      work@padring — § WILDCARD-IMPORT MATERIALIZATION (e.sv): golden
      materializes the imported package params (`work@padr.NMioPads`, with
      vpiImported) into the importing module and folds an UNQUALIFIED read of
      one in a parameter's range bound; we keep a ref_obj.  This is the
      unqualified sibling of § crossPkgRangeBoundFold and should reuse
      crossPkgBoundFoldConst9 once the materialized copies exist.

  n.sv leaves one unrelated head: `parameter logic [7:0] NSH = 'sh1f` gets an
  int_typespec (signed) in golden where we build a logic_typespec — a SIGNED
  based literal retypes the parameter.  h.sv leaves one: an UNTYPED package
  param with an unsized based default (`parameter PU = 'h3`) carries NO
  typespec in golden and size -1 in the module top view; we give it an
  int_typespec and size 32.
